# ALL.prelude -- the text corpus_suite_harness.py prefixes to the first line of every rosetta-prolog entry (SCRIP c0286d9d9).
# The package's contract with the oracle that cut its refs (hq_prolog, on the ceo's Prolog dialect ruling CEO-1632): swipl read
# a double-quoted text as a string, and these programs carry no SWI marker of their own, so they run under that flag.
:- set_prolog_flag(double_quotes, string).
# CEO-1712 (2026-10-14): and in SCRIP's SWI dialect, selected by the compile-time marker the SWI arms read (a use_module directive,
# prolog_lower.c pl_dialect_marker), as the swi_tests shim selects it.
:- use_module(library(lists)).
